---
// design/DESIGN.md §6 Tag: sans, 12px, pill, `.07` tint fill, `--ink-2` text. Flags (Preview /
// Expert area / Enterprise interest) are categorical labels on a section, not a live state, so
// they reuse Tag's plain non-semantic look rather than inventing a colored dot.
//
// The label is a slotted child, not a prop, on purpose: when `<Flags>` is used inline in a
// heading (`## Some section <Flags>Preview</Flags>`), Astro's own heading-id/table-of-contents
// extraction only ever reads a heading's *text* children — it never evaluates what a component
// renders — so a prop like `kind="preview"` would be invisible to the "on this page" nav, but
// text sitting inside the component's own tags is picked straight up alongside the heading title.
// That's what makes a flag show up next to its section in the sidebar TOC, not just in the page
// body once you've scrolled to it.
---

<span class="flag"><slot /></span>

<style>
	.flag {
		display: inline-block;
		font-size: 12px;
		font-weight: 400;
		padding: 2px 8px;
		border-radius: 999px;
		background: var(--chip);
		color: var(--ink-2);
		white-space: nowrap;
		vertical-align: middle;
	}
</style>
